    {
      "id": "p0172-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "By incorporating these language quirks into the Temmies' dialogue, the localization team ensured that Temmies sound hyper, cute, upbeat, earnest, and unique in Japanese, while also sounding weird, goofy, slightly annoying, and unintelligent. In short, Temmies are as memorable in the Japanese version of Undertale as they are in the English release.",
        "raw": "By incorporating these language quirks into the Temmies' dialogue, the\nlocalization team ensured that Temmies sound hyper, cute, upbeat, earnest,\nand unique in Japanese, while also sounding weird, goofy, slightly annoying,\nand unintelligent. In short, Temmies are as memorable in the Japanese version\nof Undertale as they are in the English release.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29982364,
          0.81159286,
          0.90465259,
          0.89682857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29530496,
          0.81087857,
          0.90669262,
          0.8979
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          51,
          52,
          53,
          54,
          55
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "把这些语言怪癖融入台词后，团队让日语 Temmie 们既亢奋、可爱、乐观、认真、独特，也古怪、傻气、有点烦人，还不太聪明。结果是：在 Undertale 日语版里，Temmie 们和英语版一样令人难忘。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
